<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kano</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kano is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> and one of the historic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa city-states</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> it became the principal commercial centre, famous for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indigo">indigo</a>-dyed textiles traded across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>. It was occupied by British forces in 1903 during the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>.</p></div>
